---
title: Path Params
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path params are used to match a single segment (the text until the next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":") and provide its value back to you as a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"named"}]},{"type":"text","value":" variable. They are defined by using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$"},{"type":"text","value":" character prefix in the path, followed by the key variable to assign it to. The following are valid path param paths:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$name"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$teamId"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"about/$name"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"team/$teamId"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blog/$postId"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because path param routes only match to the next "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":", child routes can be created to continue expressing hierarchy:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's create a post route file that uses a path param to match the post ID:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\",\"code\":\"import { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"path-params-can-be-used-by-child-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path Params can be used by child routes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once a path param has been parsed, it is available to all child routes. This means that if we define a child route to our "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postRoute"},{"type":"text","value":", we can use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postId"},{"type":"text","value":" variable from the URL in the child route's path!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"path-params-in-loaders","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path Params in Loaders"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path params are passed to the loader as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":" object. The keys of this object are the names of the path params, and the values are the values that were parsed out of the actual URL path. For example, if we were to visit the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/blog/123"},{"type":"text","value":" URL, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":" object would be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ postId: '123' }"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params"},{"type":"text","value":" object is also passed to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    // do something with params.postId\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"path-params-in-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path Params in Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If we add a component to our "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postRoute"},{"type":"text","value":", we can access the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"postId"},{"type":"text","value":" variable from the URL by using the route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useParams"},{"type":"text","value":" hook:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\\n  component: PostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction PostComponent() {\\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\\n  component: PostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction PostComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🧠 Quick tip: If your component is code-split, you can use the "},{"type":"link","href":"./code-splitting.md#manually-accessing-route-apis-in-other-files-with-the-getrouteapi-helper","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getRouteApi function"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid having to import the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"},{"type":"text","value":" configuration to get access to the typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useParams()"},{"type":"text","value":" hook."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"path-params-outside-of-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Path Params outside of Routes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also use the globally exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useParams"},{"type":"text","value":" hook to access any parsed path params from any component in your app. You'll need to pass the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strict: false"},{"type":"text","value":" option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useParams"},{"type":"text","value":", denoting that you want to access the params from an ambiguous location:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"","title":"src/components/PostComponent.tsx","file":"src/components/PostComponent.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostComponent() {\n  const params = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"","title":"src/components/PostComponent.tsx","file":"src/components/PostComponent.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostComponent() {\\n  const { postId } = useParams({ strict: false })\\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostComponent() {\\n  const params = useParams({ strict: false })\\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prioritizing-parsed-path-param-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prioritizing Parsed Path Param Routes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When multiple dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes can match the same URL, routes with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":" are tried before equivalent routes without it. If multiple matching candidates use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":", you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.priority"},{"type":"text","value":" to control which candidate is tried first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Higher "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.priority"},{"type":"text","value":" values are tried first. The default priority is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", and if a higher-priority route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", matching continues to the next candidate route."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":" runs during route planning and may be evaluated more than once.\nIt must be deterministic and side-effect-free for the same raw params."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  params: {\n    priority: 10,\n    parse: ({ postId }) => {\n      if (!/^\\d+$/.test(postId)) return false\n      return { postId: Number(postId) }\n    },\n    stringify: ({ postId }) => ({ postId: String(postId) }),\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With a fallback "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/$slug"},{"type":"text","value":" route, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/123"},{"type":"text","value":" can match the parsed numeric route first, while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/hello-world"},{"type":"text","value":" can fall through to the slug route when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.priority"},{"type":"text","value":" only affects competing candidates that use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"params.parse"},{"type":"text","value":". It does not override normal route specificity, so static routes still match before dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"navigating-with-path-params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigating with Path Params"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When navigating to a route with path params, TypeScript will require you to pass the params either as an object or as a function that returns an object of params."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let's see what an object style looks like:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And here's what a function style looks like:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={(prev) => ({ ...prev, postId: '123' })}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notice that the function style is useful when you need to persist params that are already in the URL for other routes. This is because the function style will receive the current params as an argument, allowing you to modify them as needed and return the final params object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prefixes-and-suffixes-for-path-params","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefixes and Suffixes for Path Params"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also use "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"prefixes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"suffixes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with path params to create more complex routing patterns. This allows you to match specific URL structures while still capturing the dynamic segments."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using either prefixes or suffixes, you can define them by wrapping the path param in curly braces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":" and placing the prefix or suffix before or after the variable name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"defining-prefixes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defining Prefixes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefixes are defined by placing the prefix text outside the curly braces before the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"post-"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by a post ID, you can define it like this:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {params().postId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\\n  component: PostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction PostComponent() {\\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\\n  return <div>Post ID: {postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\\n  component: PostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction PostComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\\n  return <div>Post ID: {params().postId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can even combine prefixes with wildcard routes to create more complex patterns:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{_splat}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx","file":"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{params()._splat}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx","file":"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\\n  component: StorageComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction StorageComponent() {\\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{_splat}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\\n  component: StorageComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction StorageComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{params()._splat}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"defining-suffixes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defining Suffixes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suffixes are defined by placing the suffix text outside the curly braces after the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL a filename that ends with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"txt"},{"type":"text","value":", you can define it like this:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { fileName } = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {fileName}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {params().fileName}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const { fileName } = Route.useParams()\\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\\n  return <div>File Name: {fileName}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\\n  return <div>File Name: {params().fileName}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also combine suffixes with wildcards for more complex routing patterns:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {_splat}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {params()._splat}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\\n  return <div>File Splat: {_splat}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\\n  return <div>File Splat: {params()._splat}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"combining-prefixes-and-suffixes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combining Prefixes and Suffixes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can combine both prefixes and suffixes to create very specific routing patterns. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"user-"},{"type":"text","value":" and ends with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".json"},{"type":"text","value":", you can define it like this:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {userId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx","file":"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {params().userId}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx","file":"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\\n  component: UserComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction UserComponent() {\\n  const { userId } = Route.useParams()\\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\\n  return <div>User ID: {userId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\\n  component: UserComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction UserComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\\n  return <div>User ID: {params().userId}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Similar to the previous examples, you can also use wildcards with prefixes and suffixes. Go wild!"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"optional-path-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional Path Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional path parameters allow you to define route segments that may or may not be present in the URL. They use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{-$paramName}"},{"type":"text","value":" syntax and provide flexible routing patterns where certain parameters are optional."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"defining-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defining Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional path parameters are defined using curly braces with a dash prefix: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{-$paramName}"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Single optional parameter\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  component: PostsComponent,\n})\n\n// Multiple optional parameters\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\n// Mixed required and optional parameters\n// src/routes/users/$id/{-$tab}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/$id/{-$tab}')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"how-optional-parameters-work","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How Optional Parameters Work"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters create flexible URL patterns:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/{-$category}"},{"type":"text","value":" matches both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/tech"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}"},{"type":"text","value":" matches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/tech"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/tech/hello-world"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/users/$id/{-$tab}"},{"type":"text","value":" matches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/users/123"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/users/123/settings"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When an optional parameter is not present in the URL, its value will be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" in your route handlers and components."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"accessing-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accessing Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters work exactly like regular parameters in your components, but their values may be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostsComponent() {\n  const { category } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return <div>{category ? `Posts in ${category}` : 'All Posts'}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {params().category ? `Posts in ${params().category}` : 'All Posts'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostsComponent() {\\n  const { category } = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  return <div>{category ? `Posts in ${category}` : 'All Posts'}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostsComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {params().category ? `Posts in ${params().category}` : 'All Posts'}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"optional-parameters-in-loaders","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional Parameters in Loaders"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters are available in loaders and may be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // params.category might be undefined\n    return fetchPosts({ category: params.category })\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"optional-parameters-in-beforeload","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional Parameters in beforeLoad"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters work in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" handlers as well:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    if (params.category) {\n      // Validate category exists\n      await validateCategory(params.category)\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"advanced-optional-parameter-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced Optional Parameter Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"with-prefix-and-suffix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With Prefix and Suffix"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters support prefix and suffix patterns:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { name } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {name || 'default'}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {params().name || 'default'}</div>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx","file":"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const { name } = Route.useParams()\\n  return <div>File: {name || 'default'}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\\n  component: FileComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction FileComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  return <div>File: {params().name || 'default'}</div>\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"all-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can create routes where all parameters are optional:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const { year, month, day } = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!month) return <div>Year: {year}</div>\n  if (!day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {year}/{month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {year}/{month}/{day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!params().year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!params().month) return <div>Year: {params().year}</div>\n  if (!params().day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {params().year}/{params().month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {params().year}/{params().month}/{params().day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\\n  component: DateComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction DateComponent() {\\n  const { year, month, day } = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  if (!year) return <div>Select a year</div>\\n  if (!month) return <div>Year: {year}</div>\\n  if (!day)\\n    return (\\n      <div>\\n        Month: {year}/{month}\\n      </div>\\n    )\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      Date: {year}/{month}/{day}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\\n  component: DateComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction DateComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  if (!params().year) return <div>Select a year</div>\\n  if (!params().month) return <div>Year: {params().year}</div>\\n  if (!params().day)\\n    return (\\n      <div>\\n        Month: {params().year}/{params().month}\\n      </div>\\n    )\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      Date: {params().year}/{params().month}/{params().day}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"optional-parameters-with-wildcards","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional Parameters with Wildcards"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional parameters can be combined with wildcards for complex routing patterns:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const { version } = Route.useParams()\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {version ? `v${version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {_splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx","file":"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {params().version ? `v${params().version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {params()._splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx","file":"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\\n  component: DocsComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction DocsComponent() {\\n  const { version } = Route.useParams()\\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      Version: {version ? `v${version}` : 'latest'}\\n      Path: {_splat}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\\n  component: DocsComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction DocsComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      Version: {params().version ? `v${params().version}` : 'latest'}\\n      Path: {params()._splat}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"navigating-with-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Navigating with Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When navigating to routes with optional parameters, you have fine-grained control over which parameters to include:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Navigate with optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: 'tech' }}>\n        Tech Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate without optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: undefined }}>\n        All Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate with multiple optional parameters */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}\"\n        params={{ category: 'tech', slug: 'react-tips' }}\n      >\n        Specific Post\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-safety-with-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety with Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript provides full type safety for optional parameters:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const { category } = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const params = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = params().category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostsComponent() {\\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\\n  const { category } = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\\n\\n  // Safe navigation\\n  const categoryUpper = category?.toUpperCase()\\n\\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\\n}\\n\\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\\n<Link\\n  to=\\\"/posts/{-$category}\\\"\\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\\n>\\n  Tech Posts\\n</Link>\\n\\n<Link\\n  to=\\\"/posts/{-$category}\\\"\\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\\n>\\n  Category 123\\n</Link>\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"function PostsComponent() {\\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\\n  const params = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\\n\\n  // Safe navigation\\n  const categoryUpper = params().category?.toUpperCase()\\n\\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\\n}\\n\\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\\n<Link\\n  to=\\\"/posts/{-$category}\\\"\\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\\n>\\n  Tech Posts\\n</Link>\\n\\n<Link\\n  to=\\\"/posts/{-$category}\\\"\\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\\n>\\n  Category 123\\n</Link>\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"internationalization-i18n-with-optional-path-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internationalization (i18n) with Optional Path Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional path parameters are excellent for implementing internationalization (i18n) routing patterns. You can use prefix patterns to handle multiple languages while maintaining clean, SEO-friendly URLs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"prefix-based-i18n","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix-based i18n"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use optional language prefixes to support URLs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/en/about"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/fr/about"},{"type":"text","value":", or just "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (default language):"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = params().locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$locale}/about\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\\n  component: AboutComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction AboutComponent() {\\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en' // Default to English\\n\\n  const content = {\\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\\n    fr: {\\n      title: 'À Propos',\\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\\n    },\\n    es: {\\n      title: 'Acerca de',\\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\\n    },\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$locale}/about\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\\n  component: AboutComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction AboutComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  const currentLocale = params().locale || 'en' // Default to English\\n\\n  const content = {\\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\\n    fr: {\\n      title: 'À Propos',\\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\\n    },\\n    es: {\\n      title: 'Acerca de',\\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\\n    },\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This pattern matches:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (default locale)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/en/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (explicit English)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/fr/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (French)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/es/about"},{"type":"text","value":" (Spanish)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"complex-i18n-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Complex i18n Patterns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine optional parameters for more sophisticated i18n routing:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const { locale, category, slug } = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {category || 'All'} | Language: {locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {params().category || 'All'} | Language:{' '}\n        {params().locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\\n    const category = params.category\\n\\n    // Validate locale and category\\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\\n    }\\n\\n    return { locale, category }\\n  },\\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\\n    const { locale } = context\\n    const { slug, category } = params\\n\\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\\n  },\\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\\n  const { locale, category, slug } = Route.useParams()\\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\\n\\n  return (\\n    <article>\\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\\n      <p>\\n        Category: {category || 'All'} | Language: {locale || 'en'}\\n      </p>\\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\\n    </article>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\\n    const category = params.category\\n\\n    // Validate locale and category\\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\\n    }\\n\\n    return { locale, category }\\n  },\\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\\n    const { locale } = context\\n    const { slug, category } = params\\n\\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\\n  },\\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\\n\\n  return (\\n    <article>\\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\\n      <p>\\n        Category: {params().category || 'All'} | Language:{' '}\\n        {params().locale || 'en'}\\n      </p>\\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\\n    </article>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This supports URLs like:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/blog/tech/my-post"},{"type":"text","value":" (default locale, tech category)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/fr/blog/my-post"},{"type":"text","value":" (French, no category)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/en/blog/tech/my-post"},{"type":"text","value":" (explicit English, tech category)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/es/blog/tecnologia/mi-post"},{"type":"text","value":" (Spanish, Spanish category)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"language-navigation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Language Navigation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create language switchers using optional i18n parameters with function-style params:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          key={code}\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          className={currentParams.locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"","title":"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx","file":"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          class={currentParams().locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"","title":"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx","file":"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\",\"code\":\"function LanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\\n\\n  const languages = [\\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\\n  ]\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"language-switcher\\\">\\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\\n        <Link\\n          key={code}\\n          to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n          params={(prev) => ({\\n            ...prev,\\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\\n          })}\\n          className={currentParams.locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\\n        >\\n          {name}\\n        </Link>\\n      ))}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\",\"code\":\"function LanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\\n\\n  const languages = [\\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\\n  ]\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div class=\\\"language-switcher\\\">\\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\\n        <Link\\n          to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n          params={(prev) => ({\\n            ...prev,\\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\\n          })}\\n          class={currentParams().locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\\n        >\\n          {name}\\n        </Link>\\n      ))}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also create more sophisticated language switching logic:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"function AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"function AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\\n\\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\\n    return (prev: any) => {\\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\\n\\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\\n        delete updatedParams.locale\\n      } else {\\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\\n      }\\n\\n      return updatedParams\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"language-switcher\\\">\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\\n      >\\n        Français\\n      </Link>\\n\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\\n      >\\n        Español\\n      </Link>\\n\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\\n      >\\n        English\\n      </Link>\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"function AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\\n\\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\\n    return (prev: any) => {\\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\\n\\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\\n        delete updatedParams.locale\\n      } else {\\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\\n      }\\n\\n      return updatedParams\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div class=\\\"language-switcher\\\">\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\\n      >\\n        Français\\n      </Link>\\n\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\\n      >\\n        Español\\n      </Link>\\n\\n      <Link\\n        to=\\\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\\\"\\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\\n      >\\n        English\\n      </Link>\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"advanced-i18n-with-optional-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Advanced i18n with Optional Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Organize i18n routes using optional parameters for flexible locale handling:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})","lang":"tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(params().locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({params().locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})","lang":"tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"// Route structure:\\n// routes/\\n//   {-$locale}/\\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\\n//     blog/\\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\\n\\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\\n  component: HomeComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction HomeComponent() {\\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(locale || '')\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\\n      <h1>Welcome ({locale || 'en'})</h1>\\n      {/* Localized content */}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\\n\\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\\n  component: AboutComponent,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"// Route structure:\\n// routes/\\n//   {-$locale}/\\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\\n//     blog/\\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\\n\\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\\n  component: HomeComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction HomeComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(params().locale || '')\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\\n      <h1>Welcome ({params().locale || 'en'})</h1>\\n      {/* Localized content */}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\\n\\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\\n  component: AboutComponent,\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"seo-and-canonical-urls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SEO and Canonical URLs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle SEO for i18n routes properly:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\\n  component: ProductComponent,\\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\\n    const product = loaderData\\n\\n    return {\\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\\n      meta: [\\n        {\\n          name: 'description',\\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          property: 'og:locale',\\n          content: locale,\\n        },\\n      ],\\n      links: [\\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\\n        {\\n          rel: 'canonical',\\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        // Alternate language versions\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'en',\\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'fr',\\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'es',\\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n      ],\\n    }\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\",\"code\":\"export const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\\n  component: ProductComponent,\\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\\n    const product = loaderData\\n\\n    return {\\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\\n      meta: [\\n        {\\n          name: 'description',\\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          property: 'og:locale',\\n          content: locale,\\n        },\\n      ],\\n      links: [\\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\\n        {\\n          rel: 'canonical',\\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        // Alternate language versions\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'en',\\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'fr',\\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n        {\\n          rel: 'alternate',\\n          hreflang: 'es',\\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\\n        },\\n      ],\\n    }\\n  },\\n})\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"type-safety-for-i18n","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Safety for i18n"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ensure type safety for your i18n implementations:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const { locale, category } = Route.useParams()\n  const { isDefaultLocale } = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {category ? `- ${category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const routeContext = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {params().category ? `- ${params().category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {params().locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!routeContext().isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category: params().category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"","title":"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx","file":"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx"}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"solid\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Define supported locales\\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\\n\\n// Type-safe locale validation\\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\\n}\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\\n    const { locale } = params\\n\\n    // Type-safe locale validation\\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\\n      throw redirect({\\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\\n        params: { category: params.category },\\n      })\\n    }\\n\\n    return {\\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\\n    }\\n  },\\n  component: ShopComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction ShopComponent() {\\n  const { locale, category } = Route.useParams()\\n  const { isDefaultLocale } = Route.useRouteContext()\\n\\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>Shop {category ? `- ${category}` : ''}</h1>\\n      <p>Language: {locale || 'en'}</p>\\n      {!isDefaultLocale && (\\n        <Link to=\\\"/shop/{-$category}\\\" params={{ category }}>\\n          View in English\\n        </Link>\\n      )}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\",\"code\":\"// Define supported locales\\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\\n\\n// Type-safe locale validation\\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\\n}\\n\\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\\n    const { locale } = params\\n\\n    // Type-safe locale validation\\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\\n      throw redirect({\\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\\n        params: { category: params.category },\\n      })\\n    }\\n\\n    return {\\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\\n    }\\n  },\\n  component: ShopComponent,\\n})\\n\\nfunction ShopComponent() {\\n  const params = Route.useParams()\\n  const routeContext = Route.useRouteContext()\\n\\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      <h1>Shop {params().category ? `- ${params().category}` : ''}</h1>\\n      <p>Language: {params().locale || 'en'}</p>\\n      {!routeContext().isDefaultLocale && (\\n        <Link to=\\\"/shop/{-$category}\\\" params={{ category: params().category }}>\\n          View in English\\n        </Link>\\n      )}\\n    </div>\\n  )\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional path parameters provide a powerful and flexible foundation for implementing internationalization in your TanStack Router applications. Whether you prefer prefix-based or combined approaches, you can create clean, SEO-friendly URLs while maintaining excellent developer experience and type safety."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"allowed-characters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Allowed Characters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, path params are escaped with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"encodeURIComponent"},{"type":"text","value":". If you want to allow other valid URI characters (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"+"},{"type":"text","value":"), you can specify that in your "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/router/RouterOptionsType.md#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RouterOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example usage:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This setting is fixed when the router is created. To use different allowed characters, create a new router instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following is the list of accepted allowed characters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":":"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"&"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"="}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"+"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":","}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"path-params-can-be-used-by-child-routes","text":"Path Params can be used by child routes","level":2},{"id":"path-params-in-loaders","text":"Path Params in Loaders","level":2},{"id":"path-params-in-components","text":"Path Params in Components","level":2},{"id":"path-params-outside-of-routes","text":"Path Params outside of Routes","level":2},{"id":"prioritizing-parsed-path-param-routes","text":"Prioritizing Parsed Path Param Routes","level":2},{"id":"navigating-with-path-params","text":"Navigating with Path Params","level":2},{"id":"prefixes-and-suffixes-for-path-params","text":"Prefixes and Suffixes for Path Params","level":2},{"id":"defining-prefixes","text":"Defining Prefixes","level":3},{"id":"defining-suffixes","text":"Defining Suffixes","level":3},{"id":"combining-prefixes-and-suffixes","text":"Combining Prefixes and Suffixes","level":3},{"id":"optional-path-parameters","text":"Optional Path Parameters","level":2},{"id":"defining-optional-parameters","text":"Defining Optional Parameters","level":3},{"id":"how-optional-parameters-work","text":"How Optional Parameters Work","level":3},{"id":"accessing-optional-parameters","text":"Accessing Optional Parameters","level":3},{"id":"optional-parameters-in-loaders","text":"Optional Parameters in Loaders","level":3},{"id":"optional-parameters-in-beforeload","text":"Optional Parameters in beforeLoad","level":3},{"id":"advanced-optional-parameter-patterns","text":"Advanced Optional Parameter Patterns","level":3},{"id":"with-prefix-and-suffix","text":"With Prefix and Suffix","level":4},{"id":"all-optional-parameters","text":"All Optional Parameters","level":4},{"id":"optional-parameters-with-wildcards","text":"Optional Parameters with Wildcards","level":4},{"id":"navigating-with-optional-parameters","text":"Navigating with Optional Parameters","level":3},{"id":"type-safety-with-optional-parameters","text":"Type Safety with Optional Parameters","level":3},{"id":"internationalization-i18n-with-optional-path-parameters","text":"Internationalization (i18n) with Optional Path Parameters","level":2},{"id":"prefix-based-i18n","text":"Prefix-based i18n","level":3},{"id":"complex-i18n-patterns","text":"Complex i18n Patterns","level":3},{"id":"language-navigation","text":"Language Navigation","level":3},{"id":"advanced-i18n-with-optional-parameters","text":"Advanced i18n with Optional Parameters","level":3},{"id":"seo-and-canonical-urls","text":"SEO and Canonical URLs","level":3},{"id":"type-safety-for-i18n","text":"Type Safety for i18n","level":3},{"id":"allowed-characters","text":"Allowed Characters","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","solid"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nPath params are used to match a single segment (the text until the next `/`) and provide its value back to you as a **named** variable. They are defined by using the `$` character prefix in the path, followed by the key variable to assign it to. The following are valid path param paths:\n\n- `$postId`\n- `$name`\n- `$teamId`\n- `about/$name`\n- `team/$teamId`\n- `blog/$postId`\n\nBecause path param routes only match to the next `/`, child routes can be created to continue expressing hierarchy:\n\nLet's create a post route file that uses a path param to match the post ID:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Path Params can be used by child routes\n\nOnce a path param has been parsed, it is available to all child routes. This means that if we define a child route to our `postRoute`, we can use the `postId` variable from the URL in the child route's path!\n\n## Path Params in Loaders\n\nPath params are passed to the loader as a `params` object. The keys of this object are the names of the path params, and the values are the values that were parsed out of the actual URL path. For example, if we were to visit the `/blog/123` URL, the `params` object would be `{ postId: '123' }`:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe `params` object is also passed to the `beforeLoad` option:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    // do something with params.postId\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Path Params in Components\n\nIf we add a component to our `postRoute`, we can access the `postId` variable from the URL by using the route's `useParams` hook:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> 🧠 Quick tip: If your component is code-split, you can use the [getRouteApi function](./code-splitting.md#manually-accessing-route-apis-in-other-files-with-the-getrouteapi-helper) to avoid having to import the `Route` configuration to get access to the typed `useParams()` hook.\n\n## Path Params outside of Routes\n\nYou can also use the globally exported `useParams` hook to access any parsed path params from any component in your app. You'll need to pass the `strict: false` option to `useParams`, denoting that you want to access the params from an ambiguous location:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Prioritizing Parsed Path Param Routes\n\nWhen multiple dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes can match the same URL, routes with `params.parse` are tried before equivalent routes without it. If multiple matching candidates use `params.parse`, you can use `params.priority` to control which candidate is tried first.\n\nHigher `params.priority` values are tried first. The default priority is `0`, and if a higher-priority route's `params.parse` returns `false`, matching continues to the next candidate route.\n\n`params.parse` runs during route planning and may be evaluated more than once.\nIt must be deterministic and side-effect-free for the same raw params.\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  params: {\n    priority: 10,\n    parse: ({ postId }) => {\n      if (!/^\\d+$/.test(postId)) return false\n      return { postId: Number(postId) }\n    },\n    stringify: ({ postId }) => ({ postId: String(postId) }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWith a fallback `/posts/$slug` route, `/posts/123` can match the parsed numeric route first, while `/posts/hello-world` can fall through to the slug route when `params.parse` returns `false`.\n\n`params.priority` only affects competing candidates that use `params.parse`. It does not override normal route specificity, so static routes still match before dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes.\n\n## Navigating with Path Params\n\nWhen navigating to a route with path params, TypeScript will require you to pass the params either as an object or as a function that returns an object of params.\n\nLet's see what an object style looks like:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nAnd here's what a function style looks like:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={(prev) => ({ ...prev, postId: '123' })}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nNotice that the function style is useful when you need to persist params that are already in the URL for other routes. This is because the function style will receive the current params as an argument, allowing you to modify them as needed and return the final params object.\n\n## Prefixes and Suffixes for Path Params\n\nYou can also use **prefixes** and **suffixes** with path params to create more complex routing patterns. This allows you to match specific URL structures while still capturing the dynamic segments.\n\nWhen using either prefixes or suffixes, you can define them by wrapping the path param in curly braces `{}` and placing the prefix or suffix before or after the variable name.\n\n### Defining Prefixes\n\nPrefixes are defined by placing the prefix text outside the curly braces before the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with `post-` followed by a post ID, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can even combine prefixes with wildcard routes to create more complex patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{_splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{params()._splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Defining Suffixes\n\nSuffixes are defined by placing the suffix text outside the curly braces after the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL a filename that ends with `txt`, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { fileName } = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {fileName}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {params().fileName}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can also combine suffixes with wildcards for more complex routing patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {_splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {params()._splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Combining Prefixes and Suffixes\n\nYou can combine both prefixes and suffixes to create very specific routing patterns. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with `user-` and ends with `.json`, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {userId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {params().userId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nSimilar to the previous examples, you can also use wildcards with prefixes and suffixes. Go wild!\n\n## Optional Path Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters allow you to define route segments that may or may not be present in the URL. They use the `{-$paramName}` syntax and provide flexible routing patterns where certain parameters are optional.\n\n### Defining Optional Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters are defined using curly braces with a dash prefix: `{-$paramName}`\n\n```tsx\n// Single optional parameter\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  component: PostsComponent,\n})\n\n// Multiple optional parameters\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\n// Mixed required and optional parameters\n// src/routes/users/$id/{-$tab}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/$id/{-$tab}')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n```\n\n### How Optional Parameters Work\n\nOptional parameters create flexible URL patterns:\n\n- `/posts/{-$category}` matches both `/posts` and `/posts/tech`\n- `/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}` matches `/posts`, `/posts/tech`, and `/posts/tech/hello-world`\n- `/users/$id/{-$tab}` matches `/users/123` and `/users/123/settings`\n\nWhen an optional parameter is not present in the URL, its value will be `undefined` in your route handlers and components.\n\n### Accessing Optional Parameters\n\nOptional parameters work exactly like regular parameters in your components, but their values may be `undefined`:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  const { category } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return <div>{category ? `Posts in ${category}` : 'All Posts'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {params().category ? `Posts in ${params().category}` : 'All Posts'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Optional Parameters in Loaders\n\nOptional parameters are available in loaders and may be `undefined`:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // params.category might be undefined\n    return fetchPosts({ category: params.category })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Optional Parameters in beforeLoad\n\nOptional parameters work in `beforeLoad` handlers as well:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    if (params.category) {\n      // Validate category exists\n      await validateCategory(params.category)\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Advanced Optional Parameter Patterns\n\n#### With Prefix and Suffix\n\nOptional parameters support prefix and suffix patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"\n// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { name } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {name || 'default'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"\n// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {params().name || 'default'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n#### All Optional Parameters\n\nYou can create routes where all parameters are optional:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const { year, month, day } = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!month) return <div>Year: {year}</div>\n  if (!day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {year}/{month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {year}/{month}/{day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!params().year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!params().month) return <div>Year: {params().year}</div>\n  if (!params().day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {params().year}/{params().month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {params().year}/{params().month}/{params().day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n#### Optional Parameters with Wildcards\n\nOptional parameters can be combined with wildcards for complex routing patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"\n// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const { version } = Route.useParams()\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {version ? `v${version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {_splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"\n// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {params().version ? `v${params().version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {params()._splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Navigating with Optional Parameters\n\nWhen navigating to routes with optional parameters, you have fine-grained control over which parameters to include:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Navigate with optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: 'tech' }}>\n        Tech Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate without optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: undefined }}>\n        All Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate with multiple optional parameters */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}\"\n        params={{ category: 'tech', slug: 'react-tips' }}\n      >\n        Specific Post\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Type Safety with Optional Parameters\n\nTypeScript provides full type safety for optional parameters:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const { category } = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const params = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = params().category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Internationalization (i18n) with Optional Path Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters are excellent for implementing internationalization (i18n) routing patterns. You can use prefix patterns to handle multiple languages while maintaining clean, SEO-friendly URLs.\n\n### Prefix-based i18n\n\nUse optional language prefixes to support URLs like `/en/about`, `/fr/about`, or just `/about` (default language):\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = params().locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThis pattern matches:\n\n- `/about` (default locale)\n- `/en/about` (explicit English)\n- `/fr/about` (French)\n- `/es/about` (Spanish)\n\n### Complex i18n Patterns\n\nCombine optional parameters for more sophisticated i18n routing:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const { locale, category, slug } = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {category || 'All'} | Language: {locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {params().category || 'All'} | Language:{' '}\n        {params().locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThis supports URLs like:\n\n- `/blog/tech/my-post` (default locale, tech category)\n- `/fr/blog/my-post` (French, no category)\n- `/en/blog/tech/my-post` (explicit English, tech category)\n- `/es/blog/tecnologia/mi-post` (Spanish, Spanish category)\n\n### Language Navigation\n\nCreate language switchers using optional i18n parameters with function-style params:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          key={code}\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          className={currentParams.locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          class={currentParams().locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can also create more sophisticated language switching logic:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nfunction AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nfunction AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Advanced i18n with Optional Parameters\n\nOrganize i18n routes using optional parameters for flexible locale handling:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\n// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\n// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(params().locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({params().locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### SEO and Canonical URLs\n\nHandle SEO for i18n routes properly:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Type Safety for i18n\n\nEnsure type safety for your i18n implementations:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"\n// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const { locale, category } = Route.useParams()\n  const { isDefaultLocale } = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {category ? `- ${category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"\n// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const routeContext = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {params().category ? `- ${params().category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {params().locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!routeContext().isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category: params().category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nOptional path parameters provide a powerful and flexible foundation for implementing internationalization in your TanStack Router applications. Whether you prefer prefix-based or combined approaches, you can create clean, SEO-friendly URLs while maintaining excellent developer experience and type safety.\n\n## Allowed Characters\n\nBy default, path params are escaped with `encodeURIComponent`. If you want to allow other valid URI characters (e.g. `@` or `+`), you can specify that in your [RouterOptions](../api/router/RouterOptionsType.md#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property).\n\nExample usage:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})\n```\n\nThis setting is fixed when the router is created. To use different allowed characters, create a new router instance.\n\nThe following is the list of accepted allowed characters:\n\n- `;`\n- `:`\n- `@`\n- `&`\n- `=`\n- `+`\n- `$`\n- `,`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Path Params\n---\n\nPath params are used to match a single segment (the text until the next `/`) and provide its value back to you as a **named** variable. They are defined by using the `$` character prefix in the path, followed by the key variable to assign it to. The following are valid path param paths:\n\n- `$postId`\n- `$name`\n- `$teamId`\n- `about/$name`\n- `team/$teamId`\n- `blog/$postId`\n\nBecause path param routes only match to the next `/`, child routes can be created to continue expressing hierarchy:\n\nLet's create a post route file that uses a path param to match the post ID:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/solid-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Path Params can be used by child routes\n\nOnce a path param has been parsed, it is available to all child routes. This means that if we define a child route to our `postRoute`, we can use the `postId` variable from the URL in the child route's path!\n\n## Path Params in Loaders\n\nPath params are passed to the loader as a `params` object. The keys of this object are the names of the path params, and the values are the values that were parsed out of the actual URL path. For example, if we were to visit the `/blog/123` URL, the `params` object would be `{ postId: '123' }`:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe `params` object is also passed to the `beforeLoad` option:\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    // do something with params.postId\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Path Params in Components\n\nIf we add a component to our `postRoute`, we can access the `postId` variable from the URL by using the route's `useParams` hook:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n> 🧠 Quick tip: If your component is code-split, you can use the [getRouteApi function](./code-splitting.md#manually-accessing-route-apis-in-other-files-with-the-getrouteapi-helper) to avoid having to import the `Route` configuration to get access to the typed `useParams()` hook.\n\n## Path Params outside of Routes\n\nYou can also use the globally exported `useParams` hook to access any parsed path params from any component in your app. You'll need to pass the `strict: false` option to `useParams`, denoting that you want to access the params from an ambiguous location:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/PostComponent.tsx\"\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = useParams({ strict: false })\n  return <div>Post {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Prioritizing Parsed Path Param Routes\n\nWhen multiple dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes can match the same URL, routes with `params.parse` are tried before equivalent routes without it. If multiple matching candidates use `params.parse`, you can use `params.priority` to control which candidate is tried first.\n\nHigher `params.priority` values are tried first. The default priority is `0`, and if a higher-priority route's `params.parse` returns `false`, matching continues to the next candidate route.\n\n`params.parse` runs during route planning and may be evaluated more than once.\nIt must be deterministic and side-effect-free for the same raw params.\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts.$postId.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  params: {\n    priority: 10,\n    parse: ({ postId }) => {\n      if (!/^\\d+$/.test(postId)) return false\n      return { postId: Number(postId) }\n    },\n    stringify: ({ postId }) => ({ postId: String(postId) }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nWith a fallback `/posts/$slug` route, `/posts/123` can match the parsed numeric route first, while `/posts/hello-world` can fall through to the slug route when `params.parse` returns `false`.\n\n`params.priority` only affects competing candidates that use `params.parse`. It does not override normal route specificity, so static routes still match before dynamic, optional, or wildcard routes.\n\n## Navigating with Path Params\n\nWhen navigating to a route with path params, TypeScript will require you to pass the params either as an object or as a function that returns an object of params.\n\nLet's see what an object style looks like:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={{ postId: '123' }}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nAnd here's what a function style looks like:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Component() {\n  return (\n    <Link to=\"/blog/$postId\" params={(prev) => ({ ...prev, postId: '123' })}>\n      Post 123\n    </Link>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nNotice that the function style is useful when you need to persist params that are already in the URL for other routes. This is because the function style will receive the current params as an argument, allowing you to modify them as needed and return the final params object.\n\n## Prefixes and Suffixes for Path Params\n\nYou can also use **prefixes** and **suffixes** with path params to create more complex routing patterns. This allows you to match specific URL structures while still capturing the dynamic segments.\n\nWhen using either prefixes or suffixes, you can define them by wrapping the path param in curly braces `{}` and placing the prefix or suffix before or after the variable name.\n\n### Defining Prefixes\n\nPrefixes are defined by placing the prefix text outside the curly braces before the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with `post-` followed by a post ID, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/post-{$postId}.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/post-{$postId}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction PostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // postId will be the value after 'post-'\n  return <div>Post ID: {params().postId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can even combine prefixes with wildcard routes to create more complex patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{_splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/on-disk/storage-{$postId}/$')({\n  component: StorageComponent,\n})\n\nfunction StorageComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat, will be value after 'storage-'\n  // i.e. my-drive/documents/foo.txt\n  return <div>Storage Location: /{params()._splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Defining Suffixes\n\nSuffixes are defined by placing the suffix text outside the curly braces after the variable name. For example, if you want to match a URL a filename that ends with `txt`, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { fileName } = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {fileName}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$fileName}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$fileName}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // fileName will be the value before 'txt'\n  return <div>File Name: {params().fileName}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can also combine suffixes with wildcards for more complex routing patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {_splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/{$}[.]txt.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/{$}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // _splat will be the value before '.txt'\n  return <div>File Splat: {params()._splat}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Combining Prefixes and Suffixes\n\nYou can combine both prefixes and suffixes to create very specific routing patterns. For example, if you want to match a URL that starts with `user-` and ends with `.json`, you can define it like this:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const { userId } = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {userId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/users/user-{$userId}[.]json.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/user-{$userId}.json')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n\nfunction UserComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  // userId will be the value between 'user-' and '.json'\n  return <div>User ID: {params().userId}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nSimilar to the previous examples, you can also use wildcards with prefixes and suffixes. Go wild!\n\n## Optional Path Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters allow you to define route segments that may or may not be present in the URL. They use the `{-$paramName}` syntax and provide flexible routing patterns where certain parameters are optional.\n\n### Defining Optional Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters are defined using curly braces with a dash prefix: `{-$paramName}`\n\n```tsx\n// Single optional parameter\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  component: PostsComponent,\n})\n\n// Multiple optional parameters\n// src/routes/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}')({\n  component: PostComponent,\n})\n\n// Mixed required and optional parameters\n// src/routes/users/$id/{-$tab}.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/users/$id/{-$tab}')({\n  component: UserComponent,\n})\n```\n\n### How Optional Parameters Work\n\nOptional parameters create flexible URL patterns:\n\n- `/posts/{-$category}` matches both `/posts` and `/posts/tech`\n- `/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}` matches `/posts`, `/posts/tech`, and `/posts/tech/hello-world`\n- `/users/$id/{-$tab}` matches `/users/123` and `/users/123/settings`\n\nWhen an optional parameter is not present in the URL, its value will be `undefined` in your route handlers and components.\n\n### Accessing Optional Parameters\n\nOptional parameters work exactly like regular parameters in your components, but their values may be `undefined`:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  const { category } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return <div>{category ? `Posts in ${category}` : 'All Posts'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {params().category ? `Posts in ${params().category}` : 'All Posts'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Optional Parameters in Loaders\n\nOptional parameters are available in loaders and may be `undefined`:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    // params.category might be undefined\n    return fetchPosts({ category: params.category })\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Optional Parameters in beforeLoad\n\nOptional parameters work in `beforeLoad` handlers as well:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    if (params.category) {\n      // Validate category exists\n      await validateCategory(params.category)\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Advanced Optional Parameter Patterns\n\n#### With Prefix and Suffix\n\nOptional parameters support prefix and suffix patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"\n// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const { name } = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {name || 'default'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/files/prefix{-$name}[.]txt.tsx\"\n// Route: /files/prefix{-$name}.txt\n// Matches: /files/prefix.txt and /files/prefixdocument.txt\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/files/prefix{-$name}.txt')({\n  component: FileComponent,\n})\n\nfunction FileComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  return <div>File: {params().name || 'default'}</div>\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n#### All Optional Parameters\n\nYou can create routes where all parameters are optional:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const { year, month, day } = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!month) return <div>Year: {year}</div>\n  if (!day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {year}/{month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {year}/{month}/{day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}\n// Matches: /, /2023, /2023/12, /2023/12/25\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$year}/{-$month}/{-$day}')({\n  component: DateComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DateComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  if (!params().year) return <div>Select a year</div>\n  if (!params().month) return <div>Year: {params().year}</div>\n  if (!params().day)\n    return (\n      <div>\n        Month: {params().year}/{params().month}\n      </div>\n    )\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Date: {params().year}/{params().month}/{params().day}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n#### Optional Parameters with Wildcards\n\nOptional parameters can be combined with wildcards for complex routing patterns:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"\n// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const { version } = Route.useParams()\n  const { _splat } = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {version ? `v${version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {_splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/docs/v{-$version}/$.tsx\"\n// Route: /docs/v{-$version}/$\n// Matches: /docs/extra/path, /docs/v2/extra/path\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/docs/v{-$version}/$')({\n  component: DocsComponent,\n})\n\nfunction DocsComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Version: {params().version ? `v${params().version}` : 'latest'}\n      Path: {params()._splat}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Navigating with Optional Parameters\n\nWhen navigating to routes with optional parameters, you have fine-grained control over which parameters to include:\n\n```tsx\nfunction Navigation() {\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {/* Navigate with optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: 'tech' }}>\n        Tech Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate without optional parameter */}\n      <Link to=\"/posts/{-$category}\" params={{ category: undefined }}>\n        All Posts\n      </Link>\n\n      {/* Navigate with multiple optional parameters */}\n      <Link\n        to=\"/posts/{-$category}/{-$slug}\"\n        params={{ category: 'tech', slug: 'react-tips' }}\n      >\n        Specific Post\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Type Safety with Optional Parameters\n\nTypeScript provides full type safety for optional parameters:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const { category } = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/posts/{-$category}.tsx\"\nfunction PostsComponent() {\n  // TypeScript knows category might be undefined\n  const params = Route.useParams() // category: string | undefined\n\n  // Safe navigation\n  const categoryUpper = params().category?.toUpperCase()\n\n  return <div>{categoryUpper || 'All Categories'}</div>\n}\n\n// Navigation is type-safe and flexible\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 'tech' }} // ✅ Valid - string\n>\n  Tech Posts\n</Link>\n\n<Link\n  to=\"/posts/{-$category}\"\n  params={{ category: 123 }} // ✅ Valid - number (auto-stringified)\n>\n  Category 123\n</Link>\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n## Internationalization (i18n) with Optional Path Parameters\n\nOptional path parameters are excellent for implementing internationalization (i18n) routing patterns. You can use prefix patterns to handle multiple languages while maintaining clean, SEO-friendly URLs.\n\n### Prefix-based i18n\n\nUse optional language prefixes to support URLs like `/en/about`, `/fr/about`, or just `/about` (default language):\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/about\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n\nfunction AboutComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const currentLocale = params().locale || 'en' // Default to English\n\n  const content = {\n    en: { title: 'About Us', description: 'Learn more about our company.' },\n    fr: {\n      title: 'À Propos',\n      description: 'En savoir plus sur notre entreprise.',\n    },\n    es: {\n      title: 'Acerca de',\n      description: 'Conoce más sobre nuestra empresa.',\n    },\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>{content[currentLocale]?.title}</h1>\n      <p>{content[currentLocale]?.description}</p>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThis pattern matches:\n\n- `/about` (default locale)\n- `/en/about` (explicit English)\n- `/fr/about` (French)\n- `/es/about` (Spanish)\n\n### Complex i18n Patterns\n\nCombine optional parameters for more sophisticated i18n routing:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const { locale, category, slug } = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {category || 'All'} | Language: {locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug.tsx\"\n// Route: /{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const category = params.category\n\n    // Validate locale and category\n    const validLocales = ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de']\n    if (locale && !validLocales.includes(locale)) {\n      throw new Error('Invalid locale')\n    }\n\n    return { locale, category }\n  },\n  loader: async ({ params, context }) => {\n    const { locale } = context\n    const { slug, category } = params\n\n    return fetchBlogPost({ slug, category, locale })\n  },\n  component: BlogPostComponent,\n})\n\nfunction BlogPostComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const data = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{data.title}</h1>\n      <p>\n        Category: {params().category || 'All'} | Language:{' '}\n        {params().locale || 'en'}\n      </p>\n      <div>{data.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nThis supports URLs like:\n\n- `/blog/tech/my-post` (default locale, tech category)\n- `/fr/blog/my-post` (French, no category)\n- `/en/blog/tech/my-post` (explicit English, tech category)\n- `/es/blog/tecnologia/mi-post` (Spanish, Spanish category)\n\n### Language Navigation\n\nCreate language switchers using optional i18n parameters with function-style params:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          key={code}\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          className={currentParams.locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx\"\nfunction LanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const languages = [\n    { code: 'en', name: 'English' },\n    { code: 'fr', name: 'Français' },\n    { code: 'es', name: 'Español' },\n  ]\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      {languages.map(({ code, name }) => (\n        <Link\n          to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n          params={(prev) => ({\n            ...prev,\n            locale: code === 'en' ? undefined : code, // Remove 'en' for clean URLs\n          })}\n          class={currentParams().locale === code ? 'active' : ''}\n        >\n          {name}\n        </Link>\n      ))}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nYou can also create more sophisticated language switching logic:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\nfunction AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\nfunction AdvancedLanguageSwitcher() {\n  const currentParams = useParams({ strict: false })\n\n  const handleLanguageChange = (newLocale: string) => {\n    return (prev: any) => {\n      // Preserve all existing params but update locale\n      const updatedParams = { ...prev }\n\n      if (newLocale === 'en') {\n        // Remove locale for clean English URLs\n        delete updatedParams.locale\n      } else {\n        updatedParams.locale = newLocale\n      }\n\n      return updatedParams\n    }\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div class=\"language-switcher\">\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('fr')}\n      >\n        Français\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('es')}\n      >\n        Español\n      </Link>\n\n      <Link\n        to=\"/{-$locale}/blog/{-$category}/$slug\"\n        params={handleLanguageChange('en')}\n      >\n        English\n      </Link>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Advanced i18n with Optional Parameters\n\nOrganize i18n routes using optional parameters for flexible locale handling:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx\n// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const { locale } = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx\n// Route structure:\n// routes/\n//   {-$locale}/\n//     index.tsx        // /, /en, /fr\n//     about.tsx        // /about, /en/about, /fr/about\n//     blog/\n//       index.tsx      // /blog, /en/blog, /fr/blog\n//       $slug.tsx      // /blog/post, /en/blog/post, /fr/blog/post\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/index.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/')({\n  component: HomeComponent,\n})\n\nfunction HomeComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const isRTL = ['ar', 'he', 'fa'].includes(params().locale || '')\n\n  return (\n    <div dir={isRTL ? 'rtl' : 'ltr'}>\n      <h1>Welcome ({params().locale || 'en'})</h1>\n      {/* Localized content */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\n// routes/{-$locale}/about.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/about')({\n  component: AboutComponent,\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### SEO and Canonical URLs\n\nHandle SEO for i18n routes properly:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/products/$id.tsx\"\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/products/$id')({\n  component: ProductComponent,\n  head: ({ params, loaderData }) => {\n    const locale = params.locale || 'en'\n    const product = loaderData\n\n    return {\n      title: product.title[locale] || product.title.en,\n      meta: [\n        {\n          name: 'description',\n          content: product.description[locale] || product.description.en,\n        },\n        {\n          property: 'og:locale',\n          content: locale,\n        },\n      ],\n      links: [\n        // Canonical URL (always use default locale format)\n        {\n          rel: 'canonical',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        // Alternate language versions\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'en',\n          href: `https://example.com/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'fr',\n          href: `https://example.com/fr/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n        {\n          rel: 'alternate',\n          hreflang: 'es',\n          href: `https://example.com/es/products/${params.id}`,\n        },\n      ],\n    }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\n### Type Safety for i18n\n\nEnsure type safety for your i18n implementations:\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"\n// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const { locale, category } = Route.useParams()\n  const { isDefaultLocale } = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {category ? `- ${category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n# Solid\n\n```tsx title=\"src/routes/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}.tsx\"\n// Define supported locales\ntype Locale = 'en' | 'fr' | 'es' | 'de'\n\n// Type-safe locale validation\nfunction validateLocale(locale: string | undefined): locale is Locale {\n  return ['en', 'fr', 'es', 'de'].includes(locale as Locale)\n}\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/{-$locale}/shop/{-$category}')({\n  beforeLoad: async ({ params }) => {\n    const { locale } = params\n\n    // Type-safe locale validation\n    if (locale && !validateLocale(locale)) {\n      throw redirect({\n        to: '/shop/{-$category}',\n        params: { category: params.category },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return {\n      locale: (locale as Locale) || 'en',\n      isDefaultLocale: !locale || locale === 'en',\n    }\n  },\n  component: ShopComponent,\n})\n\nfunction ShopComponent() {\n  const params = Route.useParams()\n  const routeContext = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n  // TypeScript knows locale is Locale | undefined\n  // and we have validated it in beforeLoad\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1>Shop {params().category ? `- ${params().category}` : ''}</h1>\n      <p>Language: {params().locale || 'en'}</p>\n      {!routeContext().isDefaultLocale && (\n        <Link to=\"/shop/{-$category}\" params={{ category: params().category }}>\n          View in English\n        </Link>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nOptional path parameters provide a powerful and flexible foundation for implementing internationalization in your TanStack Router applications. Whether you prefer prefix-based or combined approaches, you can create clean, SEO-friendly URLs while maintaining excellent developer experience and type safety.\n\n## Allowed Characters\n\nBy default, path params are escaped with `encodeURIComponent`. If you want to allow other valid URI characters (e.g. `@` or `+`), you can specify that in your [RouterOptions](../api/router/RouterOptionsType.md#pathparamsallowedcharacters-property).\n\nExample usage:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  // ...\n  pathParamsAllowedCharacters: ['@'],\n})\n```\n\nThis setting is fixed when the router is created. To use different allowed characters, create a new router instance.\n\nThe following is the list of accepted allowed characters:\n\n- `;`\n- `:`\n- `@`\n- `&`\n- `=`\n- `+`\n- `$`\n- `,`\n"}
